"<p>Contributions, bug reports, feature suggestions, and new marketplace templates are welcome!</p>\n<h2>Ways to Contribute</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>GitHub Repository:</strong> Explore the source code and releases at <a href=\"https://github.com/AydenGroup/nitrobase\">github.com/AydenGroup/nitrobase</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Issues &#x26; Feature Requests:</strong> Report bugs or propose features on <a href=\"https://github.com/AydenGroup/nitrobase/issues\">GitHub Issues</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>App Templates:</strong> Adding a new self-hosted app only requires adding a folder under <code>templates/&#x3C;id>/</code> with <code>template.toml</code>, <code>docker-compose.yml</code> (or upstream <code>source.path</code>), <code>logo.svg</code>, and an offline test fixture. See the <strong>Template Specification</strong> guide for details.</li>\n<li><strong>Translations:</strong> Nitrobase uses Lingui (currently English and Vietnamese). Adding a new language only requires adding its locale and translating the JSON catalog.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Before Opening a Pull Request</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Follow <a href=\"https://www.conventionalcommits.org/\">Conventional Commits</a> for commit messages.</li>\n<li>Run <code>bun run typecheck</code>, <code>bun run check</code>, and <code>bun run test</code>.</li>\n<li>If you added or changed UI or template text, run <code>bun run i18n:extract</code>, update translations, and verify with <code>bun run i18n:check</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>License</h2>\n<p>Nitrobase is released under the <strong>Functional Source License, Version 1.1, ALv2 Future License (<code>FSL-1.1-ALv2</code>)</strong>—free to use, modify, and self-host for personal, company, or client use (excluding competing services), converting automatically to <strong>Apache 2.0</strong> two years after each release.</p>"